On Apr 17, 9:54 am, MJneth...@gmail.com wrote:
> One of the things I've been noticing lately is that I accumulate
> combat wands and rarely use them.  Now part of this may be that my
> most successful characters have been, as expected for my experience,
> Barbarians, Valkyries and Samurai.  For these, it is, "If I can beat
> it up, why waste a charge on my wand?"  Even with these, though, I've
> died several times in melee with several wands unused in my
> inventory.  I typically only zap them when I get several enemies to
> line up.

Try not to die in melee.  I try to keep a wand of lightning or fire
(or digging if need be) at the ready by the time lichs are showing up
and immediately burn Elbereth.  I figure if I use up the wands then I
have less to carry.  By the end of the game you should be tripping
over wands even with a blessed bag of holding.  I figure that by the
end of the game I will have had the opportunity to easily use 30-70
wand of fire and/or lightning charges (just guessing at the number but
I figure that I find 10-20 wands of fire and lightning in a game).
So, save some Elbereth charges but otherwise use 'em up.  You can
always find more.

>
> How do you all decide when to zap and when not to?

Another thing to consider is polypiling.  If I am playing a game with
polypiling and have a bag of holding then I will keep my wands of make
invisible, slow monster, speed monster, light, etc. and polypile
them.  One time I even wound up with a 1:14 wand of death!  But
basically when polypiling wands I keep trying until they disappear or
become wands of teleportation or death.

Wands of cold can be handy for crossing water can be handy but are a
potential instadeath and there is at least one moaty-monster situation
that is guaranteed to be dangerous.  Woof-woof!

I tend to run out of digging wands on my blur through Gehennom and
need to hunt minotaurs for more wands.  I also tend to drop or poly
away my wands of striking and then not have enough charges left to
break boulders.  But it is wands of teleport and death that I covet
and I guard those until the Ascension Run where they are amazing.

Also, let me add, don't begrudge using up a charge in a wand to
engrave id it.  And if you don't get a clear result, don't begrudge
another charge in id'ing the wand.  It's far far better to id a wand
of digging (or better yet fire or lightning) early in the game than to
have it sitting in your inventory.

Good luck, good skill,
